<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>Corfu Old Town Walking Tour - Kim and Dave</name><Placemark><name>0. Start: Old Fortress bridge and Schulenburg statue</name><description>The bridge over the Contrafossa. Ship shuttles usually run to this area (check the ship's planner). Fortress: ticket, optional.</description><Point><coordinates>19.925639,39.623514,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>1. Spianada and the cricket ground</name><description>Largest square in Greece. Cricket since the British years (1814-1864).</description><Point><coordinates>19.9245,39.6238,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>1a. Kapodistrias statue and Ionian Academy (mentioned)</name><description>South end of the Spianada.</description><Point><coordinates>19.923428,39.620885,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>2. Palace of St Michael and St George (Museum of Asian Art)</name><description>North end of the Spianada. 1819-1824. Small ticket.</description><Point><coordinates>19.924781,39.625776,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>3. The Liston</name><description>French arcades of 1807 on the town side of the Spianada. Coffee and ginger beer.</description><Point><coordinates>19.923893,39.624742,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>4. Church of St Spyridon</name><description>1589; bell tower 1620. Relics of the island's patron saint. Dress modestly.</description><Point><coordinates>19.92258,39.625123,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark><Placemark><name>5. Town Hall Square (and 6. Farewell)</name><description>Town Hall (1693 loggia, theatre from 1720) and the Catholic Cathedral of St James and St Christopher.</description><Point><coordinates>19.922215,39.62341,0</coordinates></Point></Placemark></Document></kml>
